DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppppmmttooppjj reads a PPM image as input and converts it into a format  suit‐
       able to be printed by an HP PaintJet printer.

       For best results, the input file should be in 8-color RGB form; i.e. it
       should have only the 8 binary combinations of full-on and full-off pri‐
       maries.  You could convert your input to this format like this:

           pamseq 3 1 testimg.ppm >8color.pam
           pnmremap -map 8color.pam testimg.pam | ppmtopj


       Or you could use
           ppmdither -red 2 -green 2 -blue 2



OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In  addition  to  the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ),  ppppmmttooppjj  recognizes  the
       following command line options:




       --rrllee   Run length encode the image.  (This can result in larger images)


       --bbaacckk  Enhance  the foreground by indicating if the background is light
              or dark compared to the foreground.


       --rreennddeerr _a_l_g
              Use an internal rendering algorithm (default dither).


       --ggaammmmaa _i_n_t
              Gamma correct the image using the integer _i_n_t as  a  gamma  (de‐
              fault 0).


       --cceenntteerr
              Center the image to an 8.5 by 11 page


       --xxppooss _p_o_s
              Move by _p_o_s pixels in the x direction.


       --yyppooss _p_o_s
              Move by _p_o_s pixels in the y direction.




